# These fixtures are the sync token's exact bytes, so git must not rewrite
# their line endings in either direction. Without this, a checkout on Windows
# (core.autocrlf defaults on, including on GitHub's windows-latest runners)
# gets CRLF and every round-trip case compares against a trailing \r that no
# writer emits. `text eol=lf` also normalizes on commit, so an editor that
# saves CRLF cannot put one into the corpus.
*.json text eol=lf
